  "id": "Compound::DB00300 - Gene::204",
  "verbalization": "Tenofovir is linked to Ak2 through a series of molecular interactions involving Adefovir Dipivoxil, which serves as a common mediator in both the renal and Fanconi syndrome pathways. The evidence suggests that Tenofovir causes renal tubular disorders, which are ultimately linked to Adefovir Dipivoxil, and that Adefovir Dipivoxil binds to Ak2. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Tenofovir may influence Ak2 through its interaction with Adefovir Dipivoxil, which is a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor. The shared ancestry of Tenofovir and Adefovir Dipivoxil as organonitrogen compounds further supports a unified pathway. The relationship between Tenofovir and Ak2 is thus inferred through a chain of molecular interactions involving Adefovir Dipivoxil, highlighting a possible role in the broader context of drug-target interactions.",
